#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046658} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540167} :activity/id #uuid "fada443e-8034-5b67-8dc8-1b9292803e76" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049899 :topic/id #uuid "1cb109e6-3987-5c41-9a55-81f03d70697e" :topic/math-academy-id 3274} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540124 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540098 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1dc688eb-61f5-52d8-bf95-9b58a000fa0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.2138" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539537}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186539537} :answer-field/id #uuid "170b17fe-2985-5e8e-adef-2c16c5db1659" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539929}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d8455b7b-7c5b-5bab-ac5b-3afa70d37c46" :question/math-academy-id "q-224966" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(8)$ given below, compute $P(4<X\\le 6).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0138\\,$ | $\\,0.0424\\,$ | $\\,0.0996\\,$ | $\\,0.1912\\,$ | $\\,0.3134\\,$ | $\\,0.4530\\,$ | $\\,0.5925\\,$ |\n\n$P(4<X\\le 6)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(6) & =P(X\\le 6) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,6\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2,3,4\\})+P(X\\in \\{5,6\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 4)+P(4<X\\le 6) \\\\  & =F(4)+P(4<X\\le 6).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(4<X\\le 6) & =F(6)-F(4) \\\\  & =0.3134-0.0996 \\\\  & =0.2138.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "15fb34ea-7c36-5de6-89f0-352505c9199d" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540181}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540126 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167152 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad3d3640-8bab-5540-a659-263ab3ab21ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.3212" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163963} {:answer/id #uuid "bb1db4a4-1cae-534d-ad7a-abff4b20a72a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.4040" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163964} {:answer/id #uuid "24b70d04-9391-5587-a416-3485e5b2bd1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.6063" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163965} {:answer/id #uuid "2a914e27-67f8-571c-b02c-1214d09a85c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.4457" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163966} {:answer/id #uuid "3d63a520-54a9-5f47-8432-5d7d336601b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.3837" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163967}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186163967} :answer-field/id #uuid "cedfd9ab-59be-578b-9247-c2238adee679" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163962}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "74407edc-ca03-5605-ae34-cdfeb4fc24d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-224486" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(6)$ given below, compute $P(2<X\\le 5).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0620\\,$ | $\\,0.1512\\,$ | $\\,0.2851\\,$ | $\\,0.4457\\,$ | $\\,0.6063\\,$ | $\\,0.7440\\,$ | $\\,0.8472\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(5) & =P(X\\le 5) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,5\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2\\})+P(X\\in \\{3,4,5\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 2)+P(2<X\\le 5) \\\\  & =F(2)+P(2<X\\le 5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2<X\\le 5) & =F(5)-F(2) \\\\  & =0.4457-0.0620 \\\\  & =0.3837.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "296bb2e2-9a40-524a-8c06-52de5f6f888d" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540124}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540135 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540036 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "888157ba-107f-5a5c-97c9-d6b5387c773f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.6761" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539707}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186539707} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6a0816c-2f64-5562-b7f4-1cfc7a5ea04a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540018}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "27647abc-efb3-57c0-813d-ce357897815d" :question/math-academy-id "q-225086" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(9)$ given below, compute $P(X\\ge 8).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0212\\,$ | $\\,0.0550\\,$ | $\\,0.1157\\,$ | $\\,0.2068\\,$ | $\\,0.3239\\,$ | $\\,0.4557\\,$ | $\\,0.5874\\,$ |\n\n$P(X\\ge 8)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X>a)=1-P(X\\le a)=1-F(a).\n$$\n\nNow, note that \n\n$$\nP(X\\ge 8)=P(X>7).\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 8) & =P(X>7) \\\\  & =1-P(X\\le 7) \\\\  & =1-F(7) \\\\  & =1-0.3239 \\\\  & =0.6761.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "492933d6-6fda-58ce-927c-d810684d1abf"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540167 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167151 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e38d1e74-616c-5faf-bb57-5aca03f53456" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.5793" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163957} {:answer/id #uuid "0d98539a-d569-5654-b7f9-1929c49b24a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.1194" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163958} {:answer/id #uuid "0e3c8097-94e9-5fa4-b808-35465cd058b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.0241" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163959} {:answer/id #uuid "261dfc0b-c182-55d2-a867-3c1ec5a93ccd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.4599" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163960} {:answer/id #uuid "569b296c-fbd5-5a62-a832-1e70faf97df6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.3405" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163961}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186163961} :answer-field/id #uuid "41432890-ee26-58ff-bd92-b48d392c79d7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163956}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "69667702-28d4-55ff-ad76-b5f0a166efd2" :question/math-academy-id "q-224481" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(11)$ given below, compute $P(X<10).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ | $10$ | $11$ | $12$ | $13$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.1432\\,$ | $\\,0.2320\\,$ | $\\,0.3405\\,$ | $\\,0.4599\\,$ | $\\,0.5793\\,$ | $\\,0.6887\\,$ | $\\,0.7813\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<10) & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,9\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 9) \\\\  & =F(9) \\\\  & =0.3405.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "c2457db8-1ad7-55ba-80b6-98094e23625b" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540126}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540181 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540027 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9fae328c-89f2-563a-a5a4-668ae4227a93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.3007" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539747}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186539747} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2ff7417-ca9e-560f-ae90-1cd48c8905de" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539984}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "17398103-0726-57d3-aad8-24938a444c94" :question/math-academy-id "q-224994" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(7)$ given below, find the value of $P(X\\le 5).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0009\\,$ | $\\,0.0073\\,$ | $\\,0.0296\\,$ | $\\,0.0818\\,$ | $\\,0.1730\\,$ | $\\,0.3007\\,$ | $\\,0.4497\\,$ |\n\n$P(X\\le 5)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 5) & =F(5) \\\\  & =0.3007.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "fff841e9-2a22-5953-a62f-baf22457d682" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540135}}] :activity/title "The CDF of the Poisson Distribution" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539477}]}
